# What may enter a Docker build context, for the two images built from the
# repository root (`context: ..` in deploy/docker-compose.yml).
#
# This is an allowlist rather than a list of things to leave out, and that is
# the security decision in this file. The root of this repository is also where
# an operator's deployment state sits: `deploy/certs/` holds the CA key and
# every channel's client key, `deploy/vault/` holds the credential vault, and
# `.env` holds the vault's master key. A build context is not a layer — it is
# not in the published image — but it is sent to the daemon in full and is
# readable by anything that can reach a build, including a `--mount=type=bind`
# in some later stage nobody reviewed. Denying by default means the next
# directory of deployment state is excluded on the day it is created, rather
# than on the day someone remembers to add a line here.
#
# The cost is that a new workspace package has to be named below. It fails
# loudly — `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` cannot reconcile a lockfile against
# a manifest that is not there — which is the failure mode to want.

*

# The workspace's own root files. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` needs the
# lockfile and the workspace definition; `pnpm -r build` needs the base
# tsconfig every package extends.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json

# The workspace itself. `e2e` is here because it is a member of
# pnpm-workspace.yaml and the frozen lockfile covers it — it is filtered out of
# what ships by `pnpm deploy`, not by being withheld from the build.
!packages
!apps
!e2e

# Build output and installed trees, re-excluded after the directories above let
# them back in. Later patterns win, so these have to follow the `!` lines.
# Copying a host `node_modules` into the build would put the host's platform
# binaries in a Linux image, and copying a host `dist` would ship whatever was
# last built locally rather than what this Dockerfile built.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

# Never in an image, and named individually so that a reader of this file does
# not have to infer the reason from `*` above.
#
# `site/` and `design/` are outside the pnpm workspace with their own lockfiles;
# `deploy/` holds the compose file and the operator's generated key material;
# `.git` carries the full history of everything ever committed.
